> Might be off-topic, but could you explain how this works?

It is pretty primitive. I selected a fuzz input manually to start with and then asked the LLM to modify it.

<details><summary>LLM prompt (experimental)</summary>

```
› Ok, so the goal is to reach coverage in net_processing (see the diff, I've marked it, the goal is to reach that)


  I've also applied the inverse fdp from DrahtBot (you can read the repo there)



  Compiling and running the fuzz clang exe will print the fuzz seed.


  A good candidate, which hits the prior line is:


  ifdp.push_integral_in_range(1i32, 1i32, 3i32, );
  ifdp.push_integral_in_range(4395519861509i64, 0i64, 9223372036854775807i64, );
